---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Tidelet — Privacy policy" description="Tidelet does not collect any user data. Here's what that means.">
  <section>
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p><em>Last updated: 2026-04-19.</em></p>

      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <p>
        Tidelet does not collect any data about you. It runs entirely on your
        Android device, has no network permission, and talks to no servers.
        Everything you write in the app stays on your phone.
      </p>

      <h2>What data Tidelet stores</h2>
      <p>
        Your streak start date, check-ins, journal entries, thought records,
        reasons, and other notes are saved locally in an on-device database
        and in Android's DataStore. This data never leaves the device unless
        you explicitly export it yourself via Settings → Export.
      </p>

      <h2>What data Tidelet does NOT collect</h2>
      <ul class="prose-list">
        <li>No account, email address, or phone number.</li>
        <li>No advertising identifier, device identifier, or location.</li>
        <li>No analytics, crash reports, or telemetry of any kind.</li>
        <li>No third-party SDKs, trackers, or pixels.</li>
        <li>No network requests — the app does not request the Android
          <code>INTERNET</code> permission.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Backups</h2>
      <p>
        The app sets <code>android:allowBackup="false"</code>, so your data is
        not included in Google cloud backups. If you want a backup, export a
        Markdown file and store it wherever you choose.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        Tidelet is intended for adults. We do not knowingly collect data from
        anyone, including children, because we do not collect data from anyone.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions? <a href="mailto:support@tidelet.app">support@tidelet.app</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
